# Everything about this game lives in this repository — source, the press kit at
# full resolution, the soundtrack masters, and the exact build that was submitted
# to the jam. The only things kept out are the two directories that can be
# regenerated from what *is* here, plus Finder droppings.

# `npm ci` rebuilds this from the committed package-lock.json.
node_modules/

# `npm run build` rebuilds this in a second, and promo/AFTERBURN-web.zip is the
# copy that actually shipped — that one is committed.
dist/

# Where the render pipeline drops preview stills while a sequence is being
# staged. The finished mp4s and gifs land in promo/ and are committed; these are
# the hundreds of frames you look at once on the way there.
promo/titlecard2/tmp/

.DS_Store

# The no-node toolchain writes its screenshots here.
tools/tmp/

# The long-form video. Everything else made to sell this game is committed at
# full size — that rule is in the README and it is a good one — but the trailer
# is 92 MB and the two teasers are 37 MB each, and a blob that size is paid for
# by every clone forever, with no way to take it back out of history later.
# The six title cards *are* committed: they are the assets that actually get
# attached to a page or a post. Re-render these three from promo/titlecard2/
# with `await RUNFULL()` and `await RUNT('soon'|'date')`.
promo/trailer.mp4
promo/teaser-*.mp4
